.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class BOUNDARY_COMPLEX>
.br
class csmp::BoundaryInterface< dim, BOUNDARY_COMPLEX >"Policy of \fBModel\fP class for the management of internal and external boundaries which are of a lower spatial dimensional than the model and consist of \fBFace\fP objects\&. 

The \fBBoundaryInterface\fP manages the boundaries of the model, including their construction and removal\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
By contrast with the \fBRegionInterface\fP whose interfaces for \fBRegion\fP creation rely on the existance of a master region that contains all elements of the model, no such region exists for the boundaries, but boundaries are typically constructed from lower-dimensional regions tagged via the name string 'BOUNDARY' as future boundaries in the geomodelling process\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the \fBBoundaryInterface\fP is not responsible for the management of \fBFace\fP objects\&. These are handled by the \fBMeshManager\fP\&. The only thing that the \fBBoundaryInterface\fP does is to allow the creation / modification of Boundaries and to give access to them\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
S\&.K\&. Matthai 

.PP
P\&. Lang 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2010, 2017 
.RE
.PP

