.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class BOUNDARY_COMPLEX> pair< string, bool > \fBcsmp::BoundaryInterface\fP< dim, BOUNDARY_COMPLEX >::CreateBoundaryBetween (const char * group1, const char * group2)"

.PP
insert lower-dimensional \fBRegion\fP between two equidimensional unique regions, and then converts it into \fBBoundary\fP; returns boundary name Method forms a \fBBoundary\fP between the two supplied regions\&. This will involve the creation and connection of Faces\&.

.PP
This method will only work for unique Regions which are not overlapping\&.

.PP
This method makes no sense for the region '\fBModel\fP' as it encompasses all unique regions\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
returns pair singnalling the success of the operation and giving the name of the boundary\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
: BoundariesInterface cannot be created in 1D models or between regions which contain one-dimensional elements\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the BOX boundary flag will always be internal for this type of boundary because it lies between higher dimensional regions\&.
.RE
.PP
NAMING THE NEW BOUNDARY

.PP
(1\&. name of the master region from which the boundary was created if any)

.PP
.IP "2." 4
"BOUNDARY"
.IP "3." 4
the patch identifier number attached to boundary (making the boundary patch unique, avoiding duplications)
.IP "4." 4
the name of the inner region, i\&.e\&. the region that the lower-dimensional element normals point away from
.IP "5." 4
the name of the outer region, i\&.e\&. that into which the normals point
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Where the boundary just intersects a layer (same material on either side), the layer name appears only once\&. The second instance is replaced by INTERSECTION\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Attempts to create a lower-dimensional region between higher dimensional ones\&. This is done in the following steps:

.PP
.IP "0." 4
Checks:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
do the input regions exist
.IP "\(bu" 2
are they higher dimensional
.IP "\(bu" 2
is there not already a region that has the name that the new region will get?
.PP
.IP "1." 4
Using the Perimeter faces of the candiate regions, matching faces are found and the inside and outside elements are determined as well as recording their face numbers\&.
.IP "2." 4
The \fBMeshManager\fP is instructed to create the required \fBFace\fP objects AND connect them with one another\&. (no objects need to be deleted because it is assumed that there is no line element region at this boundary) 
.PP
\fBTodo\fP
.RS 4
check
.RE
.PP

.IP "3." 4
The \fBBoundary\fP is constructed from the \fBFace\fP objects\&.
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the \fBRegion\fP will be oriented such that the elements of the first region will be on the inside (normals pointing outward from this region)\&.

.PP
this region is not necessarily contiguous
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
refactored 2/4/2022 
.RE
.PP

